msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:150
msgid "**Blynk Cloud Setup and Library Imports**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:152
msgid "These lines define unique IDs and tokens required to identify and authenticate your Arduino device with the Blynk cloud. Additionally, essential libraries are imported for using the ESP8266 WiFi module, Blynk functionalities, and software serial communication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:164
msgid "**WiFi and Hardware Configuration**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:166
msgid "WiFi credentials (``ssid`` and ``pass``) are defined here. The pins ``2`` (RX) and ``3`` (TX) are set for software serial communication between the Arduino and the ESP8266. The baud rate for this communication is defined as ``115200``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:177
msgid "Define pins and global variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:179
msgid "Pins for the water pump control and soil moisture sensor are defined along with global variables to store sensor values, thresholds, modes etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:181
msgid "You need to measure your own ``moistureInAir`` and ``moistureInWater`` according to the your actual situation. To avoid the calculated ``moisturePercentage`` exceeding the range of 0-100%, adjust the ``moistureInAir`` reading upwards to account for sensor fluctuations. Conversely, adjust the ``moistureInWater`` reading downwards when recording to compensate for these fluctuations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:200
msgid "**Initial Configurations in the setup() Function**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:202
msgid "We set two timers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:204
msgid "We use ``timer.setInterval(10000L, updateDataTimer)`` to set the timer interval, here we set to execute the ``updateDataTimer()`` function every **10000ms**. You can modify the first parameter to change the interval between ``updateDataTimer()`` executions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:206
msgid "We use ``timer.setInterval(35000L, autoWaterTimer)`` to set the timer interval, here we set to execute the ``autoWaterTimer()`` function every **35000ms**. You can modify the first parameter to change the interval between ``autoWaterTimer()`` executions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:232
msgid "**loop() Function**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:234
msgid "This continuously running loop allows the Blynk library to check for updates and handles the defined timer events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:243
msgid "**Blynk App Interaction**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:245
msgid "These functions are triggered based on specific interactions with the Blynk app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:247
msgid "``BLYNK_CONNECTED()``: Called when the device connects to Blynk. Syncs the initial states of the virtual pins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:249
msgid "``BLYNK_WRITE(V1)``: Triggered when Virtual Pin 1 changes (water threshold)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:251
msgid "``BLYNK_WRITE(V2)``: Triggered when Virtual Pin 2 changes (auto mode status)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:283
msgid "**Timer Callbacks and Automatic Watering Logic**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:285
msgid "These functions handle the tasks that the timers run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:287
msgid "``updateDataTimer()``: Calls ``sendData()`` to send current moisture data to Blynk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:288
msgid "``autoWaterTimer()``: Calls ``autoWater()`` to check if watering is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:289
msgid "``sendData()``: Calculates soil moisture percentage, logs it, and sends it to the Blynk app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:290
msgid "``autoWater()``: Checks whether the soil needs watering based on the set threshold and if automatic mode is on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:339
msgid "**Pump Control Functions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:341
msgid "These functions directly control the operation of the water pump:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:343
msgid "``turnOnPump()``: Activates the pump."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/07-iot_Auto_watering_system.rst:344
msgid "``turnOffPump()``: Deactivates the pump."
msgstr ""

